Let's understand the meanings of the parts of this equation.

$\begin{align}
\boxed{\begin{align}
\scriptsize\text{Price per book}&\quad\qquad\scriptsize\text{Number of books}
\\
&\searrow\quad\qquad\swarrow
\\
&\large \underbrace{\overbrace{3}\cdot\overbrace{x}}
\\
&\qquad\uparrow
\\
&\scriptsize\text{Total price of subscription}
\end{align}}
\end{align}$

So $3x$ is the total cost of the subscription that charges per book, and so is $y$.
